CONTENT
=======

1. Guidelines: In this section we collect all conventions and rules that are
used in the 'IsaFoR/CeTA' project.
2. Compiling IsaFoR and CeTA 

1. GUIDELINES
=============

* Only commit after you checked that all thy-files still run through.
This can be done by executing:

  make

or to be on the safe side: 

  make clean && make


* Do not use CamelCase, i.e., write 'some_thm' instead of 'someThm' and
'my_new_function' instead of 'myNewFunction.'


* Do not start proofs with automated methods like

  proof (auto)

This renders proofs unmaintainable.

* For intro/elim/dest rules use suffix I/E/D, put an underscore in front of
the suffix iff the name of the lemma ends in an uppercase letter (this somehow
contradicts 1.2, but it seems to be a convention in the Isabelle libraries).


2. Compiling IsaFoR and CeTA 
============================

* Install the Glasgow Haskell Compiler (ghc).

* Install Isabelle2025 (available at http://isabelle.in.tum.de/)

* Modify your PATH variable such that $ISABELLE_HOME/bin/ is in your 
  PATH (such that "isabelle" is automatically found).

* Download and extract the corresponding version of the archive of
  formal proofs (available at https://www.isa-afp.org/)

* Edit/create your ~/.isabelle/Isabelle2025/etc/settings and add 
  the following lines (where ~ is not allowed in the path)

init_component "/the/path/to/afp/"

* Invoke isabelle once to download missing components (there are two of them)

  isabelle components -a

* Change into the root directory of the IsaFoR repository and
execute

  make

* If you wish to browse / change theories, call

  isabelle jedit -d thys -l IsaFoR_1 thys/Some_Interesting_Theory.thy

* Each directory in the thys-directory corresponds to one Isabelle session.
  The dependence between these sessions is depicted in doc/session_dependencies.tex.
  Do not create or change imports in a way that leads to a cyclic session graph!
  Each IsaFoR theory file should be listed in thys/some_session/All_of_Session.thy.
  These All_of_XXX.thy files can be regenerated by ./admin/generate_All_of_Theories.sh.
  Only invoke this script, if you have no mercurial changes. 
    
* If you want to build heap images (e.g., IsaFoR_1), use

  isabelle build -d '$ISAFOR' -b IsaFoR_1

* If you want to build a formalization on top of IsaFoR,
  add $ISAFOR to your formalization's ROOTS file.
